== General limits to the synthesis of metastable materials

Traditionally, solid state synthesis is performed at high (>1000 C) temperatures to overcome the diffusion barrier of often refractory precursors.
This yielded the belief that, in most cases, only phases stable at synthesis conditions are accesible through the solid state method, i.e. stable or remnant metastable.

